// A stand-in Hell Let Loose RCON server, wire-accurate to timraay/hllrcon's
// protocol: 12-byte LE header (magic, id, len), JSON body, XOR'd with a
// per-connection key after ServerConnect.
//
// Modes:
//   static   (default) fixed Vietnam fixtures — what hllv-rcon-selftest.ts asserts
//   dynamic  FAKE_DYNAMIC=1 — a living demo box: population follows a daily
//            curve, maps rotate on a 90-minute match clock, score and morale
//            move through the match, and the roster is generated by squad.
//            Deterministic from the wall clock, so every connection agrees and
//            a 20-second refresh shows a coherent server rather than dice.
//   game     FAKE_GAME=hll for WWII vocabulary (map ids in both grammars the
//            real game uses, WWII roles, six factions); default hllv.
//
// The dynamic mode exists so a lobby can show the module working before a
// unit has handed over its own RCON details. It is SAMPLE DATA and says so in
// the server name; nothing about it should be mistaken for a real box.
import net from "node:net";
import crypto from "node:crypto";

